    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11 Subsection 3(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nprotected IPO intercept information means information that:\n\n(a) is protected information (within the meaning of Schedule 1 to\nthe Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979);\nand\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) was obtained in accordance with an international\nproduction order issued under clause 30 or 60 of that\nSchedule; or\n\n(ii) relates to such an international production order.\nprotected IPO stored communications information means\ninformation that:\n\n(a) is protected information (within the meaning of Schedule 1 to\nthe Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979);\nand\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) was obtained in accordance with an international\nproduction order issued under clause 39 or 69 of that\nSchedule; or\n\n(ii) relates to such an international production order.\nprotected IPO telecommunications data information means\ninformation that:\n\n(a) is protected information (within the meaning of Schedule 1 to\nthe Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979);\nand\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) is telecommunications data obtained in accordance with\nan international production order; or\n\n(ii) relates to an international production order that required\nthe disclosure of telecommunications data.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\nprotected SD information means information that is protected\ninformation within the meaning of paragraph 44(1)(a), (aa), (b) or\n(c) of the Surveillance Devices Act 2004.\ntelecommunications data (except when used in Part IIIB) has the\nsame meaning as in Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\nprotected IPO intercept information means information that:\n\n(a) is protected information (within the meaning of Schedule 1 to\nthe Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979);\nand\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) was obtained in accordance with an international\nproduction order issued under clause 30 or 60 of that\nSchedule; or\n\n(ii) relates to such an international production order.\nprotected IPO stored communications information means\ninformation that:\n\n(a) is protected information (within the meaning of Schedule 1 to\nthe Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979);\nand\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) was obtained in accordance with an international\nproduction order issued under clause 39 or 69 of that\nSchedule; or\n\n(ii) relates to such an international production order.\nprotected IPO telecommunications data information means\ninformation that:\n\n(a) is protected information (within the meaning of Schedule 1 to\nthe Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979);\nand\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) is telecommunications data obtained in accordance with\nan international production order; or\n\n(ii) relates to an international production order that required\nthe disclosure of telecommunications data.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\nprotected SD information means information that is protected\ninformation within the meaning of paragraph 44(1)(a), (aa), (b) or\n(c) of the Surveillance Devices Act 2004.\ntelecommunications data (except when used in Part IIIB) has the\nsame meaning as in Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-11-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-11-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-11-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-11-logic-alleninterval-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ae34acc9d0075bb9c2b7fcfb857fa6309c239cac806571edf9e09591488a704c",
      "skos:note": "Protected information related to international production orders cannot be intercepted, stored, or accessed without a valid order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11 Subsection 3(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nprotected IPO intercept information means information that:\n\n(a) is protected information (within the meaning of Schedule 1 to\nthe Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979);\nand\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) was obtained in accordance with an international\nproduction order issued under clause 30 or 60 of that\nSchedule; or\n\n(ii) relates to such an international production order.\nprotected IPO stored communications information means\ninformation that:\n\n(a) is protected information (within the meaning of Schedule 1 to\nthe Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979);\nand\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) was obtained in accordance with an international\nproduction order issued under clause 39 or 69 of that\nSchedule; or\n\n(ii) relates to such an international production order.\nprotected IPO telecommunications data information means\ninformation that:\n\n(a) is protected information (within the meaning of Schedule 1 to\nthe Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979);\nand\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) is telecommunications data obtained in accordance with\nan international production order; or\n\n(ii) relates to an international production order that required\nthe disclosure of telecommunications data.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\nprotected SD information means information that is protected\ninformation within the meaning of paragraph 44(1)(a), (aa), (b) or\n(c) of the Surveillance Devices Act 2004.\ntelecommunications data (except when used in Part IIIB) has the\nsame meaning as in Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979."
    },
