      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(3A) Subsection (2) does not prevent an officer from divulging or\ncommunicating IPO information to an IGIS official if:\n\n(a) the information is relevant to the functions or powers of the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security; and\n\n(b) the Ombudsman is satisfied on reasonable grounds that the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security has\nsatisfactory arrangements in place for protecting the\ninformation.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(3A) Subsection (2) does not prevent an officer from divulging or\ncommunicating IPO information to an IGIS official if:\n\n(a) the information is relevant to the functions or powers of the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security; and\n\n(b) the Ombudsman is satisfied on reasonable grounds that the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security has\nsatisfactory arrangements in place for protecting the\ninformation.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-13a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-13a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "70463b9217d4e21cd2be696445fe62a83f6621ff39bca4734cd3183fd06512a6",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of IPO information to IGIS official under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-13a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13A After subsection 35(3)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(3A) Subsection (2) does not prevent an officer from divulging or\ncommunicating IPO information to an IGIS official if:\n\n(a) the information is relevant to the functions or powers of the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security; and\n\n(b) the Ombudsman is satisfied on reasonable grounds that the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security has\nsatisfactory arrangements in place for protecting the\ninformation.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
