    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-4-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 Message application service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-4-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, message application service\nmeans a service that enables end-users to send or receive messages\nto or from other end-users using a transmission service.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subclause (1), it is immaterial whether the\nservice also enables end-users to send or receive messages to or\nfrom persons (other than end-users) using a transmission service.\nExample: A webmail service that enables end-users to send emails to, or receive\nemails from, any email address.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\nmessage application service merely because the person supplies a\ntransmission service that enables messages to be sent or received.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(4) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\nmessage application service merely because the person provides a\nbilling service, or a fee collection service, in relation to a message\napplication service.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, message application service\nmeans a service that enables end-users to send or receive messages\nto or from other end-users using a transmission service.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subclause (1), it is immaterial whether the\nservice also enables end-users to send or receive messages to or\nfrom persons (other than end-users) using a transmission service.\nExample: A webmail service that enables end-users to send emails to, or receive\nemails from, any email address.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\nmessage application service merely because the person supplies a\ntransmission service that enables messages to be sent or received.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(4) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\nmessage application service merely because the person provides a\nbilling service, or a fee collection service, in relation to a message\napplication service.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-4-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
