        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-6-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2442dda9c3f2627badfb7314b32e82335b8a6d02f0dc44933f5833bb443a028d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-6-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 Video call application service",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 39,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, video call application service\nmeans a service that enables end-users to make or receive video\ncalls to or from other end-users using a transmission service.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subclause (1), it is immaterial whether the\nservice also enables end-users to make or receive video calls to or\nfrom persons (other than end-users) using a transmission service.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person does not provide a\nvideo call application service merely because the person supplies a\ntransmission service that enables video calls to be made or\nreceived.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
