    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-14-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14 Eligible judge",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-14-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, eligible Judge means a Judge in\nrelation to whom a consent under subclause (2) and a declaration\nunder subclause (3) are in force.\n\n(2) A Judge may, by writing, consent to be nominated by the\nAttorney-General under subclause (3).\n\n(3) The Attorney-General may, by writing, declare Judges in relation\nto whom consents are in force under subclause (2) to be eligible\nJudges for the purposes of this Schedule.\n\n(4) An eligible Judge has, in relation to the performance or exercise of\na function or power conferred on an eligible Judge by this\nSchedule, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the\nHigh Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, eligible Judge means a Judge in\nrelation to whom a consent under subclause (2) and a declaration\nunder subclause (3) are in force.\n\n(2) A Judge may, by writing, consent to be nominated by the\nAttorney-General under subclause (3).\n\n(3) The Attorney-General may, by writing, declare Judges in relation\nto whom consents are in force under subclause (2) to be eligible\nJudges for the purposes of this Schedule.\n\n(4) An eligible Judge has, in relation to the performance or exercise of\na function or power conferred on an eligible Judge by this\nSchedule, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the\nHigh Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-14-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-14-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-14-2-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-14-2-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c6484dbc3385d7d787b96e1aa9aa4f250e8ff0b297acdaa3089ed4503f8b5eda"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-14-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14 Eligible judge",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 43,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, eligible Judge means a Judge in\nrelation to whom a consent under subclause (2) and a declaration\nunder subclause (3) are in force.\n\n(2) A Judge may, by writing, consent to be nominated by the\nAttorney-General under subclause (3).\n\n(3) The Attorney-General may, by writing, declare Judges in relation\nto whom consents are in force under subclause (2) to be eligible\nJudges for the purposes of this Schedule.\n\n(4) An eligible Judge has, in relation to the performance or exercise of\na function or power conferred on an eligible Judge by this\nSchedule, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the\nHigh Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court."
    },
