    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17 Nominated AAT Security Division member",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may, by writing, nominate a person who:\n\n(a) holds one of the following appointments to the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal:\n\n(ii) senior member (of any level);\n\n(iii) member (of any level); and\n\n(b) is a member of the Security Division of the Administrative\nAppeals Tribunal;\nto issue international production orders under Part 4 of this\nSchedule.\n\n(2) Despite subclause (1), the Attorney-General must not nominate a\nperson who holds an appointment as a part-time senior member or\na member of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal unless the\nperson:\n\n(a) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court, of\nanother federal court or of the Supreme Court of a State or of\nthe Australian Capital Territory; and\n\n(b) has been so enrolled for not less than 5 years.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Attorney-General may, by writing, nominate a person who:\n\n(a) holds one of the following appointments to the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal:\n\n(ii) senior member (of any level);\n\n(iii) member (of any level); and\n\n(b) is a member of the Security Division of the Administrative\nAppeals Tribunal;\nto issue international production orders under Part 4 of this\nSchedule.\n\n(2) Despite subclause (1), the Attorney-General must not nominate a\nperson who holds an appointment as a part-time senior member or\na member of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal unless the\nperson:\n\n(a) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court, of\nanother federal court or of the Supreme Court of a State or of\nthe Australian Capital Territory; and\n\n(b) has been so enrolled for not less than 5 years.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-17-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-17-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dfc0c45a6e5453c98de92088c4ec76e71a050f9c140aa9d1c7fc88604b25826c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17 Nominated AAT Security Division member",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may, by writing, nominate a person who:\n\n(a) holds one of the following appointments to the\nAdministrative Appeals Tribunal:\n\n(ii) senior member (of any level);\n\n(iii) member (of any level); and\n\n(b) is a member of the Security Division of the Administrative\nAppeals Tribunal;\nto issue international production orders under Part 4 of this\nSchedule.\n\n(2) Despite subclause (1), the Attorney-General must not nominate a\nperson who holds an appointment as a part-time senior member or\na member of the Administrative Appeals Tribunal unless the\nperson:\n\n(a) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court, of\nanother federal court or of the Supreme Court of a State or of\nthe Australian Capital Territory; and\n\n(b) has been so enrolled for not less than 5 years.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
