    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-21-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-21-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.48",
      "values:originalText": "•\nAn international production order may be issued for purposes\nin connection with the investigation of an offence of a serious\nnature.\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by:\n\n(a)\nin the case of an order relating to interception—an\ninterception agency; or\n\n(b)\nin the case of an order relating to stored\ncommunications—a criminal-law enforcement agency;\nor\n\n(c)\nin the case of an order relating to telecommunications\ndata—an enforcement agency.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\nNote:\nAn international production order comes into force when it is given to\na prescribed communications provider under clause 111.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021",
      "skos:definition": "•\nAn international production order may be issued for purposes\nin connection with the investigation of an offence of a serious\nnature.\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by:\n\n(a)\nin the case of an order relating to interception—an\ninterception agency; or\n\n(b)\nin the case of an order relating to stored\ncommunications—a criminal-law enforcement agency;\nor\n\n(c)\nin the case of an order relating to telecommunications\ndata—an enforcement agency.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\nNote:\nAn international production order comes into force when it is given to\na prescribed communications provider under clause 111.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-21-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-21-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "10f77b20d2c0985c99ca7baa86da7f86ff457d537d55f3dad5a266569e6cf8fe",
      "skos:note": "International production orders may be issued for serious offence investigation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-21-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 48,
      "values:originalText": "•\nAn international production order may be issued for purposes\nin connection with the investigation of an offence of a serious\nnature.\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by:\n\n(a)\nin the case of an order relating to interception—an\ninterception agency; or\n\n(b)\nin the case of an order relating to stored\ncommunications—a criminal-law enforcement agency;\nor\n\n(c)\nin the case of an order relating to telecommunications\ndata—an enforcement agency.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\nNote:\nAn international production order comes into force when it is given to\na prescribed communications provider under clause 111.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-21-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-21-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-21-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "ISSUE",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Issue international production order.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "An international production order may be issued for purposes in connection with the investigation of an offence of a serious nature."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-22-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22 Application for international production order—enforcement of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-22-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.49",
      "values:originalText": "the criminal law\n\n(1) An interception agency may apply to an eligible Judge or\nnominated AAT member for an international production order\nunder clause 30 that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\n\n(2) The application must nominate a designated international\nagreement.\n\n(3) The application must be made on the interception agency’s behalf\nby:\n\n(a) in the case of the Australian Federal Police—a member of the\nAustralian Federal Police; or\n\n(b) in the case of the Australian Commission for Law\nEnforcement Integrity:\n\n(i) the Integrity Commissioner; or\n\n(ii) an Assistant Integrity Commissioner; or\n\n(iii) a staff member of the Australian Commission for Law\nEnforcement Integrity who is authorised in writing by\nthe Integrity Commissioner for the purposes of this\nparagraph; or\n\n(c) in the case of the ACC:\n\n(i) the Chief Executive Officer of the ACC or an examiner;\nor\n\n(ii) a member of a police force who is a member of the staff\nof the ACC; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "the criminal law\n\n(1) An interception agency may apply to an eligible Judge or\nnominated AAT member for an international production order\nunder clause 30 that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\n\n(2) The application must nominate a designated international\nagreement.\n\n(3) The application must be made on the interception agency’s behalf\nby:\n\n(a) in the case of the Australian Federal Police—a member of the\nAustralian Federal Police; or\n\n(b) in the case of the Australian Commission for Law\nEnforcement Integrity:\n\n(i) the Integrity Commissioner; or\n\n(ii) an Assistant Integrity Commissioner; or\n\n(iii) a staff member of the Australian Commission for Law\nEnforcement Integrity who is authorised in writing by\nthe Integrity Commissioner for the purposes of this\nparagraph; or\n\n(c) in the case of the ACC:\n\n(i) the Chief Executive Officer of the ACC or an examiner;\nor\n\n(ii) a member of a police force who is a member of the staff\nof the ACC; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "89a1420b145908bae01e953e6f597567f43eb5d11b77ff56043c7b3042a442dd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-22-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22 Application for international production order—enforcement of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 49,
      "values:originalText": "the criminal law\n\n(1) An interception agency may apply to an eligible Judge or\nnominated AAT member for an international production order\nunder clause 30 that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\n\n(2) The application must nominate a designated international\nagreement.\n\n(3) The application must be made on the interception agency’s behalf\nby:\n\n(a) in the case of the Australian Federal Police—a member of the\nAustralian Federal Police; or\n\n(b) in the case of the Australian Commission for Law\nEnforcement Integrity:\n\n(i) the Integrity Commissioner; or\n\n(ii) an Assistant Integrity Commissioner; or\n\n(iii) a staff member of the Australian Commission for Law\nEnforcement Integrity who is authorised in writing by\nthe Integrity Commissioner for the purposes of this\nparagraph; or\n\n(c) in the case of the ACC:\n\n(i) the Chief Executive Officer of the ACC or an examiner;\nor\n\n(ii) a member of a police force who is a member of the staff\nof the ACC; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
