      "cml:integrityHash": "380704cc1bad713911a64257bffab408c9fbf87b4fea8b45b90bc7253ee467e2",
      "skos:note": "Application must be made by authorized personnel"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22(3) Application for international production order—enforcement of",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 49,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The application must be made on the interception agency’s behalf\nby:\n\n(a) in the case of the Australian Federal Police—a member of the\nAustralian Federal Police; or\n\n(b) in the case of the Australian Commission for Law\nEnforcement Integrity:\n\n(i) the Integrity Commissioner; or\n\n(ii) an Assistant Integrity Commissioner; or\n\n(iii) a staff member of the Australian Commission for Law\nEnforcement Integrity who is authorised in writing by\nthe Integrity Commissioner for the purposes of this\nparagraph; or\n\n(c) in the case of the ACC:\n\n(i) the Chief Executive Officer of the ACC or an examiner;\nor\n\n(ii) a member of a police force who is a member of the staff\nof the ACC; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-3-norm",
