      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Authorized personnel are required to make the application",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The application must be made by authorized personnel"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "BETWEEN",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Application must be made within a specific timeframe",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "A specific timeframe is specified for making the application",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The application must be made between the specified start and end times"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-3-logic-argumentation-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "IMPLIES",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Authorized personnel are required to make the application due to their role or position",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Being a member of the Australian Federal Police, Australian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity, or ACC implies the need to make the application",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The authorized personnel must make the application because of their role or position"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-3-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "SPREADS-TO",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Application requirements spread to other entities through delegation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Delegation allows the application requirement to be applied to other entities",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The application requirement spreads to other entities through delegation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-22-2-ss-3-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "IS-A",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Application is a cognitive task for authorized personnel",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Authorized personnel are required to make the application due to their cognitive abilities",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The application is a cognitive task for authorized personnel"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-23-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23 Form of application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-23-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subclause (2), an application under clause 22 for an\ninternational production order must be in writing.\n\n(2) If the person making an application under clause 22 for an\ninternational production order on an interception agency’s behalf:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone;\nthe person may make the application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\n(3) The chief officer of an interception agency may authorise in\nwriting, for the purposes of subclause (2), persons who, or classes\nof persons who, are entitled under clause 22 to make applications\non the agency’s behalf.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subclause (2), an application under clause 22 for an\ninternational production order must be in writing.\n\n(2) If the person making an application under clause 22 for an\ninternational production order on an interception agency’s behalf:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone;\nthe person may make the application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\n(3) The chief officer of an interception agency may authorise in\nwriting, for the purposes of subclause (2), persons who, or classes\nof persons who, are entitled under clause 22 to make applications\non the agency’s behalf.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-23-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-23-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-23-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "feb5495bb7b0861951fcda8fcd3bc64b5b7cbd69df94b98f50344e10dd2c09ed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-23-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23 Form of application",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subclause (2), an application under clause 22 for an\ninternational production order must be in writing.\n\n(2) If the person making an application under clause 22 for an\ninternational production order on an interception agency’s behalf:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone;\nthe person may make the application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\n(3) The chief officer of an interception agency may authorise in\nwriting, for the purposes of subclause (2), persons who, or classes\nof persons who, are entitled under clause 22 to make applications\non the agency’s behalf."
    },
