      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the person making an application under clause 22 for an\ninternational production order on an interception agency’s behalf:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone;\nthe person may make the application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If the person making an application under clause 22 for an\ninternational production order on an interception agency’s behalf:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone;\nthe person may make the application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-23-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-23-2-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-23-2-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c43641f6bdde4aa8b00210e90d0e4ba59745b61dcbacee3c7e5b24b2c1cdc44f",
      "skos:note": "Permits making an application by telephone under urgent circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-23-2-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23(2) Form of application",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the person making an application under clause 22 for an\ninternational production order on an interception agency’s behalf:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone;\nthe person may make the application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired)."
    },
