      "skos:note": "The Queensland PIM may question a person making an application for an international production order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-29-2-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29(3) Application by interception agency of Queensland",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 54,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The Queensland PIM may, for the purpose of making submissions\nunder subclause (2), question:\n\n(a) the person making the application for the international\nproduction order on the interception agency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) a person who, under clause 27, is required by the eligible\nJudge or nominated AAT member to give further information\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\nto the eligible Judge or nominated AAT member in\nconnection with the application.\nHowever, the Queensland PIM may only do so in the presence of\nthe eligible Judge or nominated AAT member."
    },
