    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-33-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "33 Application for international production order—enforcement of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-33-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "the criminal law\n\n(1) A criminal law-enforcement agency may apply to an issuing\nauthority for an international production order under clause 39 that:\n\n(a) is in respect of a particular person; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\n\n(2) The application must nominate a designated international\nagreement.\n\n(3) The application must be made on the criminal law-enforcement\nagency’s behalf by:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subclause 22(3)—a person\nreferred to in that subclause in relation to the agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subclause (4).\n\n(4) The chief officer of the criminal law-enforcement agency may, in\nwriting, nominate for the purposes of subparagraph (3)(b)(ii) an\noffice or position in the agency that is involved in the management\nof the agency.\n\n(5) A nomination under subclause (4) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "the criminal law\n\n(1) A criminal law-enforcement agency may apply to an issuing\nauthority for an international production order under clause 39 that:\n\n(a) is in respect of a particular person; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\n\n(2) The application must nominate a designated international\nagreement.\n\n(3) The application must be made on the criminal law-enforcement\nagency’s behalf by:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subclause 22(3)—a person\nreferred to in that subclause in relation to the agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subclause (4).\n\n(4) The chief officer of the criminal law-enforcement agency may, in\nwriting, nominate for the purposes of subparagraph (3)(b)(ii) an\noffice or position in the agency that is involved in the management\nof the agency.\n\n(5) A nomination under subclause (4) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-33-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-33-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-33-2-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-33-2-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-33-2-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "89a1420b145908bae01e953e6f597567f43eb5d11b77ff56043c7b3042a442dd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-33-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "33 Application for international production order—enforcement of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "the criminal law\n\n(1) A criminal law-enforcement agency may apply to an issuing\nauthority for an international production order under clause 39 that:\n\n(a) is in respect of a particular person; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\n\n(2) The application must nominate a designated international\nagreement.\n\n(3) The application must be made on the criminal law-enforcement\nagency’s behalf by:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subclause 22(3)—a person\nreferred to in that subclause in relation to the agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subclause (4).\n\n(4) The chief officer of the criminal law-enforcement agency may, in\nwriting, nominate for the purposes of subparagraph (3)(b)(ii) an\noffice or position in the agency that is involved in the management\nof the agency.\n\n(5) A nomination under subclause (4) is not a legislative instrument."
    },
