    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-34-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "34 Form of application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-34-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.65",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application under clause 33 must be in writing.\n\n(2) However, a person making the application on the criminal\nlaw-enforcement agency’s behalf may make the application by\ntelephone if the person:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\n(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may, in\nwriting, authorise persons (including classes of persons) for the\npurposes of subclause (2). However, each person must be entitled\nunder clause 33 to make applications on the agency’s behalf.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An application under clause 33 must be in writing.\n\n(2) However, a person making the application on the criminal\nlaw-enforcement agency’s behalf may make the application by\ntelephone if the person:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\n(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may, in\nwriting, authorise persons (including classes of persons) for the\npurposes of subclause (2). However, each person must be entitled\nunder clause 33 to make applications on the agency’s behalf.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-34-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-34-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-34-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3c383c7a2844f74e1ac67600c8823b40fd061e9231dad0c2e04e8cc366ccafab"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-34-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "34 Form of application",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 65,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application under clause 33 must be in writing.\n\n(2) However, a person making the application on the criminal\nlaw-enforcement agency’s behalf may make the application by\ntelephone if the person:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\n(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may, in\nwriting, authorise persons (including classes of persons) for the\npurposes of subclause (2). However, each person must be entitled\nunder clause 33 to make applications on the agency’s behalf."
    },
