    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-43-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "43 Form of application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-43-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.73",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application under clause 42 must be in writing.\n\n(2) However, a person making the application on the enforcement\nagency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the\nperson:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\n(3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may, in writing,\nauthorise persons (including classes of persons) for the purposes of\nsubclause (2). However, each person must be entitled under clause\n42 to make applications on the agency’s behalf.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An application under clause 42 must be in writing.\n\n(2) However, a person making the application on the enforcement\nagency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the\nperson:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\n(3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may, in writing,\nauthorise persons (including classes of persons) for the purposes of\nsubclause (2). However, each person must be entitled under clause\n42 to make applications on the agency’s behalf.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-43-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-43-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-43-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7635fe66770f35d56a4e4c902b06833772e99b42890e7af902172fa30bfe4f4a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-43-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "43 Form of application",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 73,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application under clause 42 must be in writing.\n\n(2) However, a person making the application on the enforcement\nagency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the\nperson:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\n(3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may, in writing,\nauthorise persons (including classes of persons) for the purposes of\nsubclause (2). However, each person must be entitled under clause\n42 to make applications on the agency’s behalf.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
