      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.73",
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, a person making the application on the enforcement\nagency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the\nperson:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) However, a person making the application on the enforcement\nagency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the\nperson:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-43-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
