          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-43-2-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "97eeefc881512d83c5614e4b1a9dfd781c96c7e95999e9d9508056cbf3e99c40",
      "skos:note": "Telephone application permitted under urgent circumstances"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-43-2-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "43(2) Form of application",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 73,
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, a person making the application on the enforcement\nagency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the\nperson:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired)."
    },
