        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-49-ss-5-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission for indirect disclosure",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(5) A requirement under subclause (4)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the enforcement agency indirectly via the Australian Designated Authority."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-49-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "49(6) Content of international production order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-49-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "(6) For the purposes of this clause, a specified way may deal with\nmatters of timing.\nExample: If a requirement under subclause (4) relates to telecommunications\ndata that commences to be held by a prescribed communications\nprovider during a specified period, the requirement may require that\nthe telecommunications data be disclosed to the enforcement agency\nwithin 30 minutes after the telecommunications data commences to be\nheld.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) For the purposes of this clause, a specified way may deal with\nmatters of timing.\nExample: If a requirement under subclause (4) relates to telecommunications\ndata that commences to be held by a prescribed communications\nprovider during a specified period, the requirement may require that\nthe telecommunications data be disclosed to the enforcement agency\nwithin 30 minutes after the telecommunications data commences to be\nheld.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-49"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-49-ss-6-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "80163eed0d75a8ccb39c0a00cc9332e14f33bd122a14a93d33d82c8cab16647e",
      "skos:note": "Deals with matters of timing for telecommunications data disclosure."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-49-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "49(6) Content of international production order",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "(6) For the purposes of this clause, a specified way may deal with\nmatters of timing.\nExample: If a requirement under subclause (4) relates to telecommunications\ndata that commences to be held by a prescribed communications\nprovider during a specified period, the requirement may require that\nthe telecommunications data be disclosed to the enforcement agency\nwithin 30 minutes after the telecommunications data commences to be\nheld."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-49-ss-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-49-ss-6"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-50",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50 Issue of further international production order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-50"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.79",
      "values:originalText": "If:\n\n(a) an international production order (the original order) was\nissued under clause 48; and\n\n(b) the original order was directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(c) the original order relates to the investigation by an\nenforcement agency of a serious category 1 offence, or\nserious category 1 offences;\nthis Schedule does not prevent the issue of a further international\nproduction order under clause 48 that:\n\n(d) is directed to the provider; and\n\n(e) relates to the investigation by the enforcement agency of that\noffence or those offences.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "If:\n\n(a) an international production order (the original order) was\nissued under clause 48; and\n\n(b) the original order was directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(c) the original order relates to the investigation by an\nenforcement agency of a serious category 1 offence, or\nserious category 1 offences;\nthis Schedule does not prevent the issue of a further international\nproduction order under clause 48 that:\n\n(d) is directed to the provider; and\n\n(e) relates to the investigation by the enforcement agency of that\noffence or those offences.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-50-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6b8c5e486ab7fcb2ed877ff6e4c686a159361509d406c8049f9e32a9fd03d7d6",
      "skos:note": "Issue of further international production order under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-50",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50 Issue of further international production order",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 79,
      "values:originalText": "If:\n\n(a) an international production order (the original order) was\nissued under clause 48; and\n\n(b) the original order was directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider; and\n\n(c) the original order relates to the investigation by an\nenforcement agency of a serious category 1 offence, or\nserious category 1 offences;\nthis Schedule does not prevent the issue of a further international\nproduction order under clause 48 that:\n\n(d) is directed to the provider; and\n\n(e) relates to the investigation by the enforcement agency of that\noffence or those offences.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-50-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-50"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-51",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-51"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "•\nIf a control order is in force in relation to a person, an\ninternational production order may be issued for purposes in\nconnection with the monitoring of the person, so as to protect\nthe public from terrorist acts, prevent support for terrorist acts\nand hostile acts overseas and detect breaches of the control\norder.\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by a control order IPO agency.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\n•\nIf an international production order is issued in relation to an\napplication made by a control order IPO agency, the agency\nmust notify the international production order to the\nOmbudsman.\nNote:\nAn international production order comes into force when it is given to\na prescribed communications provider under clause 111.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021",
      "skos:definition": "•\nIf a control order is in force in relation to a person, an\ninternational production order may be issued for purposes in\nconnection with the monitoring of the person, so as to protect\nthe public from terrorist acts, prevent support for terrorist acts\nand hostile acts overseas and detect breaches of the control\norder.\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by a control order IPO agency.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\n•\nIf an international production order is issued in relation to an\napplication made by a control order IPO agency, the agency\nmust notify the international production order to the\nOmbudsman.\nNote:\nAn international production order comes into force when it is given to\na prescribed communications provider under clause 111.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-51-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "caf67bec137768727435b3a65c97fb27a0fede6cc71c3320d7236a5714538e21",
      "skos:note": "International production orders for monitoring purposes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-51",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "•\nIf a control order is in force in relation to a person, an\ninternational production order may be issued for purposes in\nconnection with the monitoring of the person, so as to protect\nthe public from terrorist acts, prevent support for terrorist acts\nand hostile acts overseas and detect breaches of the control\norder.\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by a control order IPO agency.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\n•\nIf an international production order is issued in relation to an\napplication made by a control order IPO agency, the agency\nmust notify the international production order to the\nOmbudsman.\nNote:\nAn international production order comes into force when it is given to\na prescribed communications provider under clause 111.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-51-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-51"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-52",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52 Application for international production order—control order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-52"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.81",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A control order IPO agency may apply to an eligible Judge or\nnominated AAT member for an international production order\nunder clause 60 that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\n\n(2) The application must nominate a designated international\nagreement.\n\n(3) The application must be made on the control order IPO agency’s\nbehalf by:\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subclause 22(3)—a person\nreferred to in that subclause in relation to the agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subclause (4).\n\n(4) The chief officer of the control order IPO agency may, in writing,\nnominate for the purposes of subparagraph (3)(b)(ii) an office or\nposition in the agency that is involved in the management of the\nagency.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A control order IPO agency may apply to an eligible Judge or\nnominated AAT member for an international production order\nunder clause 60 that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\n\n(2) The application must nominate a designated international\nagreement.\n\n(3) The application must be made on the control order IPO agency’s\nbehalf by:\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subclause 22(3)—a person\nreferred to in that subclause in relation to the agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subclause (4).\n\n(4) The chief officer of the control order IPO agency may, in writing,\nnominate for the purposes of subparagraph (3)(b)(ii) an office or\nposition in the agency that is involved in the management of the\nagency.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-52-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-52-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-52-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-52-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aa5dc61d35fd9e09e9f268632ceadb5a4dba8bfcdba09f04a37d537538957c5b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-52",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52 Application for international production order—control order",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 81,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A control order IPO agency may apply to an eligible Judge or\nnominated AAT member for an international production order\nunder clause 60 that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\n\n(2) The application must nominate a designated international\nagreement.\n\n(3) The application must be made on the control order IPO agency’s\nbehalf by:\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subclause 22(3)—a person\nreferred to in that subclause in relation to the agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subclause (4).\n\n(4) The chief officer of the control order IPO agency may, in writing,\nnominate for the purposes of subparagraph (3)(b)(ii) an office or\nposition in the agency that is involved in the management of the\nagency."
    },
    {
