    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-58",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58 Application by control order IPO agency of Victoria",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-58"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies if a control order IPO agency of Victoria\napplies, under clause 52, to an eligible Judge or nominated AAT\nmember for an international production order under clause 60 that\nis in respect of:\n\n(a) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(b) one or more individual message/call application services.\nPIM may make submissions\n\n(2) A Victorian PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to\nthe eligible Judge or nominated AAT member about the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual transmission\nservices—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 60(5)(a) to\n(g);\n\n(b) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual message/call\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\napplication services—the matters mentioned in paragraphs\n60(6)(a) to (g).\nPIM may question certain persons\n\n(3) The Victorian PIM may, for the purpose of making submissions\nunder subclause (2), question:\n\n(a) the person making the application for the international\nproduction order on the control order IPO agency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) a person who, under clause 57, is required by the eligible\nJudge or nominated AAT member to give further information\nto the eligible Judge or nominated AAT member in\nconnection with the application.\nHowever, the Victorian PIM may only do so in the presence of the\neligible Judge or nominated AAT member.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies if a control order IPO agency of Victoria\napplies, under clause 52, to an eligible Judge or nominated AAT\nmember for an international production order under clause 60 that\nis in respect of:\n\n(a) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(b) one or more individual message/call application services.\nPIM may make submissions\n\n(2) A Victorian PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to\nthe eligible Judge or nominated AAT member about the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual transmission\nservices—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 60(5)(a) to\n(g);\n\n(b) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual message/call\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\napplication services—the matters mentioned in paragraphs\n60(6)(a) to (g).\nPIM may question certain persons\n\n(3) The Victorian PIM may, for the purpose of making submissions\nunder subclause (2), question:\n\n(a) the person making the application for the international\nproduction order on the control order IPO agency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) a person who, under clause 57, is required by the eligible\nJudge or nominated AAT member to give further information\nto the eligible Judge or nominated AAT member in\nconnection with the application.\nHowever, the Victorian PIM may only do so in the presence of the\neligible Judge or nominated AAT member.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-58-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-58-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-58-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-58",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58 Application by control order IPO agency of Victoria",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies if a control order IPO agency of Victoria\napplies, under clause 52, to an eligible Judge or nominated AAT\nmember for an international production order under clause 60 that\nis in respect of:\n\n(a) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(b) one or more individual message/call application services.\nPIM may make submissions\n\n(2) A Victorian PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to\nthe eligible Judge or nominated AAT member about the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual transmission\nservices—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 60(5)(a) to\n(g);\n\n(b) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual message/call\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\napplication services—the matters mentioned in paragraphs\n60(6)(a) to (g).\nPIM may question certain persons\n\n(3) The Victorian PIM may, for the purpose of making submissions\nunder subclause (2), question:\n\n(a) the person making the application for the international\nproduction order on the control order IPO agency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) a person who, under clause 57, is required by the eligible\nJudge or nominated AAT member to give further information\nto the eligible Judge or nominated AAT member in\nconnection with the application.\nHowever, the Victorian PIM may only do so in the presence of the\neligible Judge or nominated AAT member."
    },
