    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-59-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "59(2) Application by control order IPO agency of Queensland",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-59-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.85",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A Queensland PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to\nthe eligible Judge or nominated AAT member about the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual transmission\nservices—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 60(5)(a) to\n(g);\n\n(b) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual message/call\napplication services—the matters mentioned in paragraphs\n60(6)(a) to (g).\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A Queensland PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to\nthe eligible Judge or nominated AAT member about the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual transmission\nservices—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 60(5)(a) to\n(g);\n\n(b) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual message/call\napplication services—the matters mentioned in paragraphs\n60(6)(a) to (g).\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-59"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-59-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-59-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9862feeb1c930ee43455b9fa106f4b187e7d643d489d5e0e292521c0bad5ad72",
      "skos:note": "A Queensland PIM may make submissions to the eligible Judge or nominated AAT member."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-59-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "59(2) Application by control order IPO agency of Queensland",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 85,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A Queensland PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to\nthe eligible Judge or nominated AAT member about the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual transmission\nservices—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 60(5)(a) to\n(g);\n\n(b) in the case of an application for an international production\norder that is in respect of one or more individual message/call\napplication services—the matters mentioned in paragraphs\n60(6)(a) to (g).\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
