      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b8437dd94a701062a11d068f85647c14f5abb330767982a893217fad063fa39a",
      "skos:note": "Exempting intercepted messages from direct availability to IPO agency"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-61-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "61(7) Content of international production order",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "(7) A requirement under subclause (6) may:\n\n(a) require that intercepted messages, voice calls or video calls\nbe made available to the control order IPO agency directly;\nor\n\n(b) require that intercepted messages, voice calls or video calls\nbe made available to the control order IPO agency indirectly\nvia the Australian Designated Authority."
    },
