    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-73",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "73 Form of application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-73"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.108",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application under clause 72 must be in writing.\n\n(2) However, a person making the application on the control order IPO\nagency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the\nperson:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(3) The chief officer of a control order IPO agency may, in writing,\nauthorise persons (including classes of persons) for the purposes of\nsubclause (2). However, each person must be entitled under clause\n72 to make applications on the agency’s behalf.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An application under clause 72 must be in writing.\n\n(2) However, a person making the application on the control order IPO\nagency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the\nperson:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(3) The chief officer of a control order IPO agency may, in writing,\nauthorise persons (including classes of persons) for the purposes of\nsubclause (2). However, each person must be entitled under clause\n72 to make applications on the agency’s behalf.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-73-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-73-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-73-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "134c006adb18187e56b5b970508b56d0dc72ce6fa4e55b795bb865d9095117ef"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-73",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "73 Form of application",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 108,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application under clause 72 must be in writing.\n\n(2) However, a person making the application on the control order IPO\nagency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the\nperson:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubclause (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\nNote:\nSee also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action\nrequired).\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(3) The chief officer of a control order IPO agency may, in writing,\nauthorise persons (including classes of persons) for the purposes of\nsubclause (2). However, each person must be entitled under clause\n72 to make applications on the agency’s behalf."
    },
