      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-81",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "81 Notification to Ombudsman by control order IPO agencies in",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-81"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.116",
      "values:originalText": "relation to international production orders\n\n(1) Within 3 months after an international production order is issued\nunder this Part in response to an application by a control order IPO\nagency, the chief officer of the agency must:\n\n(a) notify the Ombudsman that the order has been issued; and\n\n(b) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the order.\n\n(2) If the chief officer of a control order IPO agency contravenes\nparagraph 114(1)(d) of this Schedule (so far as that paragraph\nrelates to an international production order issued under this Part),\nthe chief officer must:\n\n(a) notify the Ombudsman of the contravention; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the contravention.\n\n(3) A failure to comply with subclause (1) or (2) does not affect the\nvalidity of an international production order.",
      "skos:definition": "relation to international production orders\n\n(1) Within 3 months after an international production order is issued\nunder this Part in response to an application by a control order IPO\nagency, the chief officer of the agency must:\n\n(a) notify the Ombudsman that the order has been issued; and\n\n(b) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the order.\n\n(2) If the chief officer of a control order IPO agency contravenes\nparagraph 114(1)(d) of this Schedule (so far as that paragraph\nrelates to an international production order issued under this Part),\nthe chief officer must:\n\n(a) notify the Ombudsman of the contravention; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the contravention.\n\n(3) A failure to comply with subclause (1) or (2) does not affect the\nvalidity of an international production order.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-81-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-81-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-81-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "84eac76313330a622d64f42e8dcb8dd14304b8e5017426895ff9f689d270d36b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-81",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "81 Notification to Ombudsman by control order IPO agencies in",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 116,
      "values:originalText": "relation to international production orders\n\n(1) Within 3 months after an international production order is issued\nunder this Part in response to an application by a control order IPO\nagency, the chief officer of the agency must:\n\n(a) notify the Ombudsman that the order has been issued; and\n\n(b) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the order.\n\n(2) If the chief officer of a control order IPO agency contravenes\nparagraph 114(1)(d) of this Schedule (so far as that paragraph\nrelates to an international production order issued under this Part),\nthe chief officer must:\n\n(a) notify the Ombudsman of the contravention; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the contravention.\n\n(3) A failure to comply with subclause (1) or (2) does not affect the\nvalidity of an international production order."
    },
