    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-82",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "82 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-82"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.116",
      "values:originalText": "•\nInternational production orders may be issued for purposes in\nconnection with the carrying out by the Organisation of its\nfunctions.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by the Organisation.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\nNote:\nAn international production order comes into force when it is given to\na prescribed communications provider under clause 112.",
      "skos:definition": "•\nInternational production orders may be issued for purposes in\nconnection with the carrying out by the Organisation of its\nfunctions.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by the Organisation.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\nNote:\nAn international production order comes into force when it is given to\na prescribed communications provider under clause 112.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-82-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a8f253f7abc3bea50931afb0a619ea605b6ebfd548db71e773fec345a3aa70ee",
      "skos:note": "International production orders may be issued for purposes in connection with the carrying out by the Organisation of its functions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-82",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "82 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 116,
      "values:originalText": "•\nInternational production orders may be issued for purposes in\nconnection with the carrying out by the Organisation of its\nfunctions.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n•\nThere are 3 types of international production orders:\n\n(a)\ninternational production orders relating to interception;\nand\n\n(b)\ninternational production orders relating to stored\ncommunications; and\n\n(c)\ninternational production orders relating to\ntelecommunications data.\n•\nAn international production order is directed to a prescribed\ncommunications provider.\n•\nAn international production order may be issued in response\nto an application made by the Organisation.\n•\nAn application for an international production order must\nnominate a designated international agreement.\nNote:\nAn international production order comes into force when it is given to\na prescribed communications provider under clause 112."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-82-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-82"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-83",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "83 Application for international production order—national",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-83"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.117",
      "values:originalText": "security\n\n(1) The Organisation may apply to a nominated AAT Security\nDivision member for an international production order under\nclause 89 that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\n\n(2) The application must nominate a designated international\nagreement.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "security\n\n(1) The Organisation may apply to a nominated AAT Security\nDivision member for an international production order under\nclause 89 that:\n\n(a) is in respect of:\n\n(i) one or more individual transmission services; or\n\n(ii) one or more individual message/call application\nservices; and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\n\n(2) The application must nominate a designated international\nagreement.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
