    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-107",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "107 Issue of international production order—national security",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-107"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.143",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies if the Organisation applies, under clause 101, to\na nominated AAT Security Division member for an international\nproduction order that:\n\n(a) is in respect of a particular person (the relevant person); and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\nIssue of international production order\n\n(2) If the nominated AAT Security Division member is satisfied, on\nthe basis of the information given to the nominated AAT Security\nDivision member under this Division in connection with the\napplication, that:\n\n(a) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the\nprescribed communications provider holds, or is likely to\ncommence to hold, any of the following telecommunications\ndata:\n\n(i) telecommunications data that relates to communications\nthat the relevant person has made using an individual\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies if the Organisation applies, under clause 101, to\na nominated AAT Security Division member for an international\nproduction order that:\n\n(a) is in respect of a particular person (the relevant person); and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\nIssue of international production order\n\n(2) If the nominated AAT Security Division member is satisfied, on\nthe basis of the information given to the nominated AAT Security\nDivision member under this Division in connection with the\napplication, that:\n\n(a) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the\nprescribed communications provider holds, or is likely to\ncommence to hold, any of the following telecommunications\ndata:\n\n(i) telecommunications data that relates to communications\nthat the relevant person has made using an individual\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-107-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-107-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-107",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "107 Issue of international production order—national security",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 143,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies if the Organisation applies, under clause 101, to\na nominated AAT Security Division member for an international\nproduction order that:\n\n(a) is in respect of a particular person (the relevant person); and\n\n(b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.\nIssue of international production order\n\n(2) If the nominated AAT Security Division member is satisfied, on\nthe basis of the information given to the nominated AAT Security\nDivision member under this Division in connection with the\napplication, that:\n\n(a) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the\nprescribed communications provider holds, or is likely to\ncommence to hold, any of the following telecommunications\ndata:\n\n(i) telecommunications data that relates to communications\nthat the relevant person has made using an individual\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
