      "cml:premiseText": "National security grounds exist",
      "cml:conclusionText": "State must investigate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-108",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "108 Content of international production order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-108"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.146",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies to an international production order issued\nunder clause 107.\nContent\n\n(2) The order must be signed by the nominated AAT Security Division\nmember who issued it.\n\n(3) The order must set out the following:\n\n(a) the date on which the order was issued;\n\n(b) the name of the prescribed communications provider to\nwhom the order is directed;\n\n(c) the name of the designated international agreement\nnominated in the application for the order.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(4) If the order directs a prescribed communications provider to\ndisclose telecommunications data to the Organisation, the order\nmay require the provider to disclose that data to the Organisation in\na specified way.\n\n(5) A requirement under subclause (4) may:\n\n(a) require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the\nOrganisation directly; or\n\n(b) require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the\nOrganisation indirectly via the Australian Designated\nAuthority.\n\n(6) For the purposes of this clause, a specified way may deal with\nmatters of timing.\nExample: If a requirement under subclause (4) relates to telecommunications\ndata that commences to be held by a prescribed communications\nprovider during a specified period, the requirement may require that\nthe telecommunications data be disclosed to the Organisation within\n30 minutes after the telecommunications data commences to be held.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies to an international production order issued\nunder clause 107.\nContent\n\n(2) The order must be signed by the nominated AAT Security Division\nmember who issued it.\n\n(3) The order must set out the following:\n\n(a) the date on which the order was issued;\n\n(b) the name of the prescribed communications provider to\nwhom the order is directed;\n\n(c) the name of the designated international agreement\nnominated in the application for the order.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(4) If the order directs a prescribed communications provider to\ndisclose telecommunications data to the Organisation, the order\nmay require the provider to disclose that data to the Organisation in\na specified way.\n\n(5) A requirement under subclause (4) may:\n\n(a) require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the\nOrganisation directly; or\n\n(b) require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the\nOrganisation indirectly via the Australian Designated\nAuthority.\n\n(6) For the purposes of this clause, a specified way may deal with\nmatters of timing.\nExample: If a requirement under subclause (4) relates to telecommunications\ndata that commences to be held by a prescribed communications\nprovider during a specified period, the requirement may require that\nthe telecommunications data be disclosed to the Organisation within\n30 minutes after the telecommunications data commences to be held.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-108-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-108-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-108-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-108-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-108-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-108-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-108",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "108 Content of international production order",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 146,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This clause applies to an international production order issued\nunder clause 107.\nContent\n\n(2) The order must be signed by the nominated AAT Security Division\nmember who issued it.\n\n(3) The order must set out the following:\n\n(a) the date on which the order was issued;\n\n(b) the name of the prescribed communications provider to\nwhom the order is directed;\n\n(c) the name of the designated international agreement\nnominated in the application for the order.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(4) If the order directs a prescribed communications provider to\ndisclose telecommunications data to the Organisation, the order\nmay require the provider to disclose that data to the Organisation in\na specified way.\n\n(5) A requirement under subclause (4) may:\n\n(a) require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the\nOrganisation directly; or\n\n(b) require that the telecommunications data be disclosed to the\nOrganisation indirectly via the Australian Designated\nAuthority.\n\n(6) For the purposes of this clause, a specified way may deal with\nmatters of timing.\nExample: If a requirement under subclause (4) relates to telecommunications\ndata that commences to be held by a prescribed communications\nprovider during a specified period, the requirement may require that\nthe telecommunications data be disclosed to the Organisation within\n30 minutes after the telecommunications data commences to be held."
    },
