    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-113",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "113 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-113"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.151",
      "values:originalText": "•\nIf an international production order was issued in response to\nan application made by a relevant agency, the chief officer of\nthe agency:\n\n(a)\nmay revoke the order; and\n\n(b)\nmust revoke the order if the chief officer is satisfied that\nthe grounds on which the order was issued have ceased\nto exist.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "•\nIf an international production order was issued in response to\nan application made by a relevant agency, the chief officer of\nthe agency:\n\n(a)\nmay revoke the order; and\n\n(b)\nmust revoke the order if the chief officer is satisfied that\nthe grounds on which the order was issued have ceased\nto exist.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-113-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-113-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c909b51399eaf8c3326057b963319552845ba0091e9eb9805902eb5f144b6182",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer must revoke order if grounds cease to exist."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-113",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "113 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 151,
      "values:originalText": "•\nIf an international production order was issued in response to\nan application made by a relevant agency, the chief officer of\nthe agency:\n\n(a)\nmay revoke the order; and\n\n(b)\nmust revoke the order if the chief officer is satisfied that\nthe grounds on which the order was issued have ceased\nto exist.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-113-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-113"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-113-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide revocation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-114",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "114 Revocation of international production orders—relevant agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-114"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.152",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order was issued under Part 2 or 3\nof this Schedule; and\n\n(b) the order was issued in response to an application made by a\nrelevant agency;\nthe chief officer of the agency:\n\n(c) may revoke the order; and\n\n(d) must revoke the order if the chief officer is satisfied that the\ngrounds on which the order was issued have ceased to exist.\n\n(2) A revocation under this clause is to be set out in a written\ninstrument.\n\n(3) For the purposes of the application of subclause (1) to an\ninternational production order issued under Part 3 of this Schedule\non the ground that a control order was in force in relation to a\nparticular person when the international production order was\nissued, that ground is taken to have ceased to exist if, and only if,\nneither that control order, nor any succeeding control order, is in\nforce.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order was issued under Part 2 or 3\nof this Schedule; and\n\n(b) the order was issued in response to an application made by a\nrelevant agency;\nthe chief officer of the agency:\n\n(c) may revoke the order; and\n\n(d) must revoke the order if the chief officer is satisfied that the\ngrounds on which the order was issued have ceased to exist.\n\n(2) A revocation under this clause is to be set out in a written\ninstrument.\n\n(3) For the purposes of the application of subclause (1) to an\ninternational production order issued under Part 3 of this Schedule\non the ground that a control order was in force in relation to a\nparticular person when the international production order was\nissued, that ground is taken to have ceased to exist if, and only if,\nneither that control order, nor any succeeding control order, is in\nforce.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-114-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-114-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-114-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a91634d010eaaf0ac1a33941c2a19b89b1262b481947ae834598a8e746d9bbd2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-114",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "114 Revocation of international production orders—relevant agency",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 152,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) an international production order was issued under Part 2 or 3\nof this Schedule; and\n\n(b) the order was issued in response to an application made by a\nrelevant agency;\nthe chief officer of the agency:\n\n(c) may revoke the order; and\n\n(d) must revoke the order if the chief officer is satisfied that the\ngrounds on which the order was issued have ceased to exist.\n\n(2) A revocation under this clause is to be set out in a written\ninstrument.\n\n(3) For the purposes of the application of subclause (1) to an\ninternational production order issued under Part 3 of this Schedule\non the ground that a control order was in force in relation to a\nparticular person when the international production order was\nissued, that ground is taken to have ceased to exist if, and only if,\nneither that control order, nor any succeeding control order, is in\nforce.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021"
    },
    {
