    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-117-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "117(4) Giving of instrument of revocation—the Organisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-117-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.154",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\n(a) an international production order is revoked under clause\n116; and\n\n(b) when the revocation takes effect, the Australian Designated\nAuthority has not made a decision about the order under\nclause 112;\nclause 112 ceases to apply to the order when the revocation takes\neffect.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If:\n\n(a) an international production order is revoked under clause\n116; and\n\n(b) when the revocation takes effect, the Australian Designated\nAuthority has not made a decision about the order under\nclause 112;\nclause 112 ceases to apply to the order when the revocation takes\neffect.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-117"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-117-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-117-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e8030afd737c2eec96cbacf771530652ea983e8413c0f243a8b251eac1a39e74",
      "skos:note": "Revocation of international production order"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-117-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "117(4) Giving of instrument of revocation—the Organisation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 154,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\n(a) an international production order is revoked under clause\n116; and\n\n(b) when the revocation takes effect, the Australian Designated\nAuthority has not made a decision about the order under\nclause 112;\nclause 112 ceases to apply to the order when the revocation takes\neffect.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021"
    },
