      "cml:premiseText": "Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Relevant courts for civil penalty provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-127",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "127 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-127"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "•\nThe chief officer of a relevant agency and the Australian\nDesignated Authority must give the Minister annual reports\nabout matters relating to international production orders.\n•\nThe Director-General of Security must give the\nAttorney-General a report on the extent to which compliance\nby a prescribed communications provider with an international\nproduction order has assisted the Organisation in carrying out\nits functions.\n•\nThe Minister must cause to be prepared annual reports about\nmatters relating to international production orders that were\nissued in response to applications made by relevant agencies.\n•\nThe chief officer of a relevant agency, the Director-General of\nSecurity and the Australian Designated Authority must ensure\nthat records are kept of matters relating to international\nproduction orders.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021",
      "skos:definition": "•\nThe chief officer of a relevant agency and the Australian\nDesignated Authority must give the Minister annual reports\nabout matters relating to international production orders.\n•\nThe Director-General of Security must give the\nAttorney-General a report on the extent to which compliance\nby a prescribed communications provider with an international\nproduction order has assisted the Organisation in carrying out\nits functions.\n•\nThe Minister must cause to be prepared annual reports about\nmatters relating to international production orders that were\nissued in response to applications made by relevant agencies.\n•\nThe chief officer of a relevant agency, the Director-General of\nSecurity and the Australian Designated Authority must ensure\nthat records are kept of matters relating to international\nproduction orders.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-127-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-127-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ee23996d817506c51e655c926752df416a74af1fa8826e674f6e338b484f9574",
      "skos:note": "Annual reports must be given by certain agencies and authorities.",
      "dc:description": "annual reports"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-127",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "127 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 160,
      "values:originalText": "•\nThe chief officer of a relevant agency and the Australian\nDesignated Authority must give the Minister annual reports\nabout matters relating to international production orders.\n•\nThe Director-General of Security must give the\nAttorney-General a report on the extent to which compliance\nby a prescribed communications provider with an international\nproduction order has assisted the Organisation in carrying out\nits functions.\n•\nThe Minister must cause to be prepared annual reports about\nmatters relating to international production orders that were\nissued in response to applications made by relevant agencies.\n•\nThe chief officer of a relevant agency, the Director-General of\nSecurity and the Australian Designated Authority must ensure\nthat records are kept of matters relating to international\nproduction orders.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-127-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
