    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-130",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "130 Annual reports by the Australian Designated Authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-130"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.163",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Australian Designated Authority must, within 3 months after\nthe end of each financial year, give the Minister a written report\nthat sets out, for each relevant agency:\n\n(a) if one or more international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency were given by\nthe Australian Designated Authority to prescribed\ncommunications providers during the financial year:\n\n(i) the number of those orders; and\n\n(ii) the number of each type of those orders; and\n\n(iii) for each designated international agreement—the\nnumber of those orders that invoked the designated\ninternational agreement; and\n\n(b) if subparagraph 30(2)(g)(ii) or (h)(ii) applied to one or more\ninternational production orders that were:\n\n(i) issued under clause 30 in response to applications made\nby the agency; and\n\n(ii) given by the Australian Designated Authority to\nprescribed communications providers during the\nfinancial year;\n\nthe number of those orders; and\n\n(c) if subparagraph 60(2)(g)(ii) or (h)(ii) applied to one or more\ninternational production orders that were:\n\n(i) issued under clause 60 in response to applications made\nby the agency; and\n\n(ii) given by the Australian Designated Authority to\nprescribed communications providers during the\nfinancial year;\n\nthe number of those orders; and\n\n(d) if one or more international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency were cancelled\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Australian Designated Authority must, within 3 months after\nthe end of each financial year, give the Minister a written report\nthat sets out, for each relevant agency:\n\n(a) if one or more international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency were given by\nthe Australian Designated Authority to prescribed\ncommunications providers during the financial year:\n\n(i) the number of those orders; and\n\n(ii) the number of each type of those orders; and\n\n(iii) for each designated international agreement—the\nnumber of those orders that invoked the designated\ninternational agreement; and\n\n(b) if subparagraph 30(2)(g)(ii) or (h)(ii) applied to one or more\ninternational production orders that were:\n\n(i) issued under clause 30 in response to applications made\nby the agency; and\n\n(ii) given by the Australian Designated Authority to\nprescribed communications providers during the\nfinancial year;\n\nthe number of those orders; and\n\n(c) if subparagraph 60(2)(g)(ii) or (h)(ii) applied to one or more\ninternational production orders that were:\n\n(i) issued under clause 60 in response to applications made\nby the agency; and\n\n(ii) given by the Australian Designated Authority to\nprescribed communications providers during the\nfinancial year;\n\nthe number of those orders; and\n\n(d) if one or more international production orders issued in\nresponse to applications made by the agency were cancelled\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-130-norm"
        },
