    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-133",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "133 Keeping documents associated with international production",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-133"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.169",
      "values:originalText": "orders—relevant agencies\n\n(1) The chief officer of a relevant agency must cause the following to\nbe kept in the agency’s records:\n\n(a) a copy of each written application made by the agency for an\ninternational production order;\n\n(b) a copy of each affidavit that accompanied a written\napplication made by the agency for an international\nproduction order;\n\n(c) a copy of each international production order issued in\nresponse to an application made by the agency;\n\n(d) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 23(3);\n\n(e) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 34(3);\n\n(f) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 43(3);\n\n(g) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 53(3);\n\n(h) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 64(3);\n\n(i) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 73(3);\n\n(j) if the chief officer revokes an international production order\nunder clause 114—a copy of the instrument of revocation.\n\n(2) The period for which the chief officer of a relevant agency must\ncause a copy of a particular document to be kept in the agency’s\nrecords under subclause (1) is the period:\n\n(a) starting when the document came into existence; and\n\n(b) ending:\n\n(i) when 3 years have elapsed since the document came\ninto existence; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "orders—relevant agencies\n\n(1) The chief officer of a relevant agency must cause the following to\nbe kept in the agency’s records:\n\n(a) a copy of each written application made by the agency for an\ninternational production order;\n\n(b) a copy of each affidavit that accompanied a written\napplication made by the agency for an international\nproduction order;\n\n(c) a copy of each international production order issued in\nresponse to an application made by the agency;\n\n(d) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 23(3);\n\n(e) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 34(3);\n\n(f) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 43(3);\n\n(g) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 53(3);\n\n(h) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 64(3);\n\n(i) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 73(3);\n\n(j) if the chief officer revokes an international production order\nunder clause 114—a copy of the instrument of revocation.\n\n(2) The period for which the chief officer of a relevant agency must\ncause a copy of a particular document to be kept in the agency’s\nrecords under subclause (1) is the period:\n\n(a) starting when the document came into existence; and\n\n(b) ending:\n\n(i) when 3 years have elapsed since the document came\ninto existence; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-133-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-133-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "df6f616903150b9e38cf6aa07f5db4c534cea2ff4df909171568e0518fdf0ce8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-133",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "133 Keeping documents associated with international production",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 169,
      "values:originalText": "orders—relevant agencies\n\n(1) The chief officer of a relevant agency must cause the following to\nbe kept in the agency’s records:\n\n(a) a copy of each written application made by the agency for an\ninternational production order;\n\n(b) a copy of each affidavit that accompanied a written\napplication made by the agency for an international\nproduction order;\n\n(c) a copy of each international production order issued in\nresponse to an application made by the agency;\n\n(d) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 23(3);\n\n(e) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 34(3);\n\n(f) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 43(3);\n\n(g) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 53(3);\n\n(h) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 64(3);\n\n(i) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under\nsubclause 73(3);\n\n(j) if the chief officer revokes an international production order\nunder clause 114—a copy of the instrument of revocation.\n\n(2) The period for which the chief officer of a relevant agency must\ncause a copy of a particular document to be kept in the agency’s\nrecords under subclause (1) is the period:\n\n(a) starting when the document came into existence; and\n\n(b) ending:\n\n(i) when 3 years have elapsed since the document came\ninto existence; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
