      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.169",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The period for which the chief officer of a relevant agency must\ncause a copy of a particular document to be kept in the agency’s\nrecords under subclause (1) is the period:\n\n(a) starting when the document came into existence; and\n\n(b) ending:\n\n(i) when 3 years have elapsed since the document came\ninto existence; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The period for which the chief officer of a relevant agency must\ncause a copy of a particular document to be kept in the agency’s\nrecords under subclause (1) is the period:\n\n(a) starting when the document came into existence; and\n\n(b) ending:\n\n(i) when 3 years have elapsed since the document came\ninto existence; or\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
