      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.180",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If:\n\n(a) an international production order was issued in response to an\napplication made by a relevant agency; and\n\n(b) in compliance with the order, a prescribed communications\nprovider makes a copy of stored communications available to\nthe agency (whether directly or indirectly via the Australian\nDesignated Authority); and\n\n(c) the copy is in the agency’s possession; and\n\n(d) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the copy is not\nlikely to be required for a purpose referred to in clause 153 or\n158;\nthe chief officer must cause the copy to be destroyed immediately\nafter becoming so satisfied.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If:\n\n(a) an international production order was issued in response to an\napplication made by a relevant agency; and\n\n(b) in compliance with the order, a prescribed communications\nprovider makes a copy of stored communications available to\nthe agency (whether directly or indirectly via the Australian\nDesignated Authority); and\n\n(c) the copy is in the agency’s possession; and\n\n(d) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the copy is not\nlikely to be required for a purpose referred to in clause 153 or\n158;\nthe chief officer must cause the copy to be destroyed immediately\nafter becoming so satisfied.",
