    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-141",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "141 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-141"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.182",
      "values:originalText": "•\nThe Ombudsman may inspect records of a relevant agency to\ndetermine the extent of compliance with this Schedule by the\nrelevant agency and its officers.\n•\nThe Ombudsman may inspect records of the Australian\nDesignated Authority to determine the extent of compliance\nwith this Schedule by the Australian Designated Authority.\n•\nThe Ombudsman must give the Minister an annual report\nabout the results of those inspections.",
      "skos:definition": "•\nThe Ombudsman may inspect records of a relevant agency to\ndetermine the extent of compliance with this Schedule by the\nrelevant agency and its officers.\n•\nThe Ombudsman may inspect records of the Australian\nDesignated Authority to determine the extent of compliance\nwith this Schedule by the Australian Designated Authority.\n•\nThe Ombudsman must give the Minister an annual report\nabout the results of those inspections.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-141-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-141-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "837388b6f33c4e916b0a27206356be1f5225643b4c93c7c1d177b784b09fd8bf",
      "skos:note": "Inspect records to determine compliance with the Schedule.",
      "dc:description": "Annual report to the Minister"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-141",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "141 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 182,
      "values:originalText": "•\nThe Ombudsman may inspect records of a relevant agency to\ndetermine the extent of compliance with this Schedule by the\nrelevant agency and its officers.\n•\nThe Ombudsman may inspect records of the Australian\nDesignated Authority to determine the extent of compliance\nwith this Schedule by the Australian Designated Authority.\n•\nThe Ombudsman must give the Minister an annual report\nabout the results of those inspections."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-141-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-141"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-141-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to inspect records",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-142",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "142 Inspection of records—relevant agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-142"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.182",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman may inspect records of a relevant agency to\ndetermine the extent of compliance with this Schedule by the\nrelevant agency and its officers.\n\n(2) For the purpose of an inspection under this clause, the\nOmbudsman:\n\n(a) after notifying the chief officer of the relevant agency, may\nenter at any reasonable time premises occupied by the\nrelevant agency; and\n\n(b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times\nto all records of the relevant agency that are relevant to the\ninspection; and\n\n(c) despite any other law, is entitled to make copies of, and to\ntake extracts from, records of the relevant agency; and\n\n(d) may require a member of staff of the relevant agency to give\nthe Ombudsman any information that the Ombudsman\nconsiders necessary, being information:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(i) that is in the member’s possession, or to which the\nmember has access; and\n\n(ii) that is relevant to the inspection.\n\n(3) Before inspecting records of a relevant agency under this clause,\nthe Ombudsman must give reasonable notice to the chief officer of\nthe relevant agency of when the inspection will occur.\n\n(4) The chief officer must ensure that members of staff of the relevant\nagency give the Ombudsman any assistance the Ombudsman\nreasonably requires to enable the Ombudsman to perform functions\nunder this clause.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Ombudsman may inspect records of a relevant agency to\ndetermine the extent of compliance with this Schedule by the\nrelevant agency and its officers.\n\n(2) For the purpose of an inspection under this clause, the\nOmbudsman:\n\n(a) after notifying the chief officer of the relevant agency, may\nenter at any reasonable time premises occupied by the\nrelevant agency; and\n\n(b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times\nto all records of the relevant agency that are relevant to the\ninspection; and\n\n(c) despite any other law, is entitled to make copies of, and to\ntake extracts from, records of the relevant agency; and\n\n(d) may require a member of staff of the relevant agency to give\nthe Ombudsman any information that the Ombudsman\nconsiders necessary, being information:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(i) that is in the member’s possession, or to which the\nmember has access; and\n\n(ii) that is relevant to the inspection.\n\n(3) Before inspecting records of a relevant agency under this clause,\nthe Ombudsman must give reasonable notice to the chief officer of\nthe relevant agency of when the inspection will occur.\n\n(4) The chief officer must ensure that members of staff of the relevant\nagency give the Ombudsman any assistance the Ombudsman\nreasonably requires to enable the Ombudsman to perform functions\nunder this clause.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-142-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-142-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-142-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-142-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "33c42d6e74331e10dfa47c60e48d420ea13b108cd2cfb2c33c1c7b7a34d06c1f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-142",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "142 Inspection of records—relevant agency",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 182,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman may inspect records of a relevant agency to\ndetermine the extent of compliance with this Schedule by the\nrelevant agency and its officers.\n\n(2) For the purpose of an inspection under this clause, the\nOmbudsman:\n\n(a) after notifying the chief officer of the relevant agency, may\nenter at any reasonable time premises occupied by the\nrelevant agency; and\n\n(b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times\nto all records of the relevant agency that are relevant to the\ninspection; and\n\n(c) despite any other law, is entitled to make copies of, and to\ntake extracts from, records of the relevant agency; and\n\n(d) may require a member of staff of the relevant agency to give\nthe Ombudsman any information that the Ombudsman\nconsiders necessary, being information:\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(i) that is in the member’s possession, or to which the\nmember has access; and\n\n(ii) that is relevant to the inspection.\n\n(3) Before inspecting records of a relevant agency under this clause,\nthe Ombudsman must give reasonable notice to the chief officer of\nthe relevant agency of when the inspection will occur.\n\n(4) The chief officer must ensure that members of staff of the relevant\nagency give the Ombudsman any assistance the Ombudsman\nreasonably requires to enable the Ombudsman to perform functions\nunder this clause."
    },
