    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-143",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "143 Inspection of records—Australian Designated Authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-143"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.183",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman may inspect records of the Australian Designated\nAuthority to determine the extent of compliance with this Schedule\nby the Australian Designated Authority.\n\n(2) For the purpose of an inspection under this clause, the\nOmbudsman:\n\n(a) after notifying the Australian Designated Authority, may\nenter at any reasonable time premises occupied by the\nAttorney-General’s Department; and\n\n(b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times\nto all records of the Australian Designated Authority that are\nrelevant to the inspection; and\n\n(c) despite any other law, is entitled to make copies of, and to\ntake extracts from, records of the Australian Designated\nAuthority; and\n\n(d) may require a member of staff of the Attorney-General’s\nDepartment to give the Ombudsman any information that the\nOmbudsman considers necessary, being information:\n\n(i) that is in the member’s possession, or to which the\nmember has access; and\n\n(ii) that is relevant to the inspection.\n\n(3) Before inspecting records of the Australian Designated Authority\nunder this clause, the Ombudsman must give reasonable notice to\nthe Australian Designated Authority of when the inspection will\noccur.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Ombudsman may inspect records of the Australian Designated\nAuthority to determine the extent of compliance with this Schedule\nby the Australian Designated Authority.\n\n(2) For the purpose of an inspection under this clause, the\nOmbudsman:\n\n(a) after notifying the Australian Designated Authority, may\nenter at any reasonable time premises occupied by the\nAttorney-General’s Department; and\n\n(b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times\nto all records of the Australian Designated Authority that are\nrelevant to the inspection; and\n\n(c) despite any other law, is entitled to make copies of, and to\ntake extracts from, records of the Australian Designated\nAuthority; and\n\n(d) may require a member of staff of the Attorney-General’s\nDepartment to give the Ombudsman any information that the\nOmbudsman considers necessary, being information:\n\n(i) that is in the member’s possession, or to which the\nmember has access; and\n\n(ii) that is relevant to the inspection.\n\n(3) Before inspecting records of the Australian Designated Authority\nunder this clause, the Ombudsman must give reasonable notice to\nthe Australian Designated Authority of when the inspection will\noccur.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-143-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-143-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-143-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a0e362c2d6fbaf6e89443d6d026248df5d5a2c6003688a34aa2474879eaa59b9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-143",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "143 Inspection of records—Australian Designated Authority",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 183,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman may inspect records of the Australian Designated\nAuthority to determine the extent of compliance with this Schedule\nby the Australian Designated Authority.\n\n(2) For the purpose of an inspection under this clause, the\nOmbudsman:\n\n(a) after notifying the Australian Designated Authority, may\nenter at any reasonable time premises occupied by the\nAttorney-General’s Department; and\n\n(b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times\nto all records of the Australian Designated Authority that are\nrelevant to the inspection; and\n\n(c) despite any other law, is entitled to make copies of, and to\ntake extracts from, records of the Australian Designated\nAuthority; and\n\n(d) may require a member of staff of the Attorney-General’s\nDepartment to give the Ombudsman any information that the\nOmbudsman considers necessary, being information:\n\n(i) that is in the member’s possession, or to which the\nmember has access; and\n\n(ii) that is relevant to the inspection.\n\n(3) Before inspecting records of the Australian Designated Authority\nunder this clause, the Ombudsman must give reasonable notice to\nthe Australian Designated Authority of when the inspection will\noccur.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
