    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-157",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "157 Exceptions—international production orders relating to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-157"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.194",
      "values:originalText": "interception\n\n(1) Protected information that:\n\n(a) was obtained in accordance with an international production\norder issued under clause 30, 60 or 89; or\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(b) relates to an international production order issued under\nclause 30, 60 or 89;\nmay be used, recorded or disclosed, or may be admitted in\nevidence, for any of the following purposes:\n\n(c) a proceeding for the confiscation or forfeiture of property in\nconnection with the commission of a serious category 1\noffence;\n\n(d) a proceeding under the Spam Act 2003;\n\n(e) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, the main unexplained wealth provisions;\n\n(f) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, the unexplained wealth legislation of a\nparticipating State, the Australian Capital Territory or the\nNorthern Territory;\n\n(g) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, an organised crime control law;\n\n(h) a proceeding for the extradition of a person from a State or\nTerritory to another State or Territory, in so far as the\nproceeding relates to a serious category 1 offence;\n\n(i) a proceeding by way of a coroner’s inquest if, in the opinion\nof the coroner, the event that is the subject of the inquest may\nhave resulted from the commission of a serious category 1\noffence;\n\n(j) a police disciplinary proceeding;\n\n(k) a proceeding in so far as it relates to:\n\n(i) a decision by the Commissioner of Police to terminate\nthe employment of an AFP employee or the\nappointment of a special member of the Australian\nFederal Police; or\n\n(ii) a decision by the Commissioner of a Police Force of a\nState to terminate the appointment of an officer or\nmember of staff of that Police Force;\n\n(l) a proceeding in so far as it is, or relates to, disciplinary or\nlegal action (within the meaning of section 6S) that is in\nrelation to an eligible staff member (within the meaning of\nthat section) of the Australian Federal Police or the ACC;\n\n(m) any other proceeding (not being a proceeding by way of a\nprosecution for an offence) in so far as it relates to alleged\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "interception\n\n(1) Protected information that:\n\n(a) was obtained in accordance with an international production\norder issued under clause 30, 60 or 89; or\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(b) relates to an international production order issued under\nclause 30, 60 or 89;\nmay be used, recorded or disclosed, or may be admitted in\nevidence, for any of the following purposes:\n\n(c) a proceeding for the confiscation or forfeiture of property in\nconnection with the commission of a serious category 1\noffence;\n\n(d) a proceeding under the Spam Act 2003;\n\n(e) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, the main unexplained wealth provisions;\n\n(f) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, the unexplained wealth legislation of a\nparticipating State, the Australian Capital Territory or the\nNorthern Territory;\n\n(g) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, an organised crime control law;\n\n(h) a proceeding for the extradition of a person from a State or\nTerritory to another State or Territory, in so far as the\nproceeding relates to a serious category 1 offence;\n\n(i) a proceeding by way of a coroner’s inquest if, in the opinion\nof the coroner, the event that is the subject of the inquest may\nhave resulted from the commission of a serious category 1\noffence;\n\n(j) a police disciplinary proceeding;\n\n(k) a proceeding in so far as it relates to:\n\n(i) a decision by the Commissioner of Police to terminate\nthe employment of an AFP employee or the\nappointment of a special member of the Australian\nFederal Police; or\n\n(ii) a decision by the Commissioner of a Police Force of a\nState to terminate the appointment of an officer or\nmember of staff of that Police Force;\n\n(l) a proceeding in so far as it is, or relates to, disciplinary or\nlegal action (within the meaning of section 6S) that is in\nrela",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-157-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-157-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "afd9643141a9003f54a20a6f03673abdc88fb11f81f410ca1a512b4a16186163",
      "skos:note": "Protected information can be used, recorded or disclosed for specific purposes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-157",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "157 Exceptions—international production orders relating to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 194,
      "values:originalText": "interception\n\n(1) Protected information that:\n\n(a) was obtained in accordance with an international production\norder issued under clause 30, 60 or 89; or\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021\n\n(b) relates to an international production order issued under\nclause 30, 60 or 89;\nmay be used, recorded or disclosed, or may be admitted in\nevidence, for any of the following purposes:\n\n(c) a proceeding for the confiscation or forfeiture of property in\nconnection with the commission of a serious category 1\noffence;\n\n(d) a proceeding under the Spam Act 2003;\n\n(e) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, the main unexplained wealth provisions;\n\n(f) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, the unexplained wealth legislation of a\nparticipating State, the Australian Capital Territory or the\nNorthern Territory;\n\n(g) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, an organised crime control law;\n\n(h) a proceeding for the extradition of a person from a State or\nTerritory to another State or Territory, in so far as the\nproceeding relates to a serious category 1 offence;\n\n(i) a proceeding by way of a coroner’s inquest if, in the opinion\nof the coroner, the event that is the subject of the inquest may\nhave resulted from the commission of a serious category 1\noffence;\n\n(j) a police disciplinary proceeding;\n\n(k) a proceeding in so far as it relates to:\n\n(i) a decision by the Commissioner of Police to terminate\nthe employment of an AFP employee or the\nappointment of a special member of the Australian\nFederal Police; or\n\n(ii) a decision by the Commissioner of a Police Force of a\nState to terminate the appointment of an officer or\nmember of staff of that Police Force;\n\n(l) a proceeding in so far as it is, or relates to, disciplinary or\nlegal action (within the meaning of section 6S) that is in\nrelation to an eligible staff member (within the meaning of\nthat section) of the Australian Federal Police or the ACC;\n\n(m) any other proceeding (not being a proceeding by way of a\nprosecution for an offence) in so far as it relates to alleged\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-157-norm",
