      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-167",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "167 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-167"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.217",
      "values:originalText": "•\nIf there is a designated international agreement between\nAustralia and one or more foreign countries, and a competent\nauthority of such a foreign country issues an order, or makes a\nrequest, covered by the agreement, an act or thing done in\ncompliance with such an order or request is exempt from:\n\n(a)\nthe provisions of this Act that prohibit intercepting\ncommunications and accessing stored communications;\nand\n\n(b)\nthe provisions of this Act that prohibit disclosure of\ninformation; and\n\n(c)\nthe provisions of the Telecommunications Act 1997 that\nprohibit the disclosure of information.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "•\nIf there is a designated international agreement between\nAustralia and one or more foreign countries, and a competent\nauthority of such a foreign country issues an order, or makes a\nrequest, covered by the agreement, an act or thing done in\ncompliance with such an order or request is exempt from:\n\n(a)\nthe provisions of this Act that prohibit intercepting\ncommunications and accessing stored communications;\nand\n\n(b)\nthe provisions of this Act that prohibit disclosure of\ninformation; and\n\n(c)\nthe provisions of the Telecommunications Act 1997 that\nprohibit the disclosure of information.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-167-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-167-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "88fdb19602c061aefb3e66c3275d9e41795bae2568ef5a76fb10e62895becea1",
      "skos:note": "Exemption from certain provisions for acts done in compliance with foreign country orders or requests under international agreements."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-167",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "167 Simplified outline of this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 217,
      "values:originalText": "•\nIf there is a designated international agreement between\nAustralia and one or more foreign countries, and a competent\nauthority of such a foreign country issues an order, or makes a\nrequest, covered by the agreement, an act or thing done in\ncompliance with such an order or request is exempt from:\n\n(a)\nthe provisions of this Act that prohibit intercepting\ncommunications and accessing stored communications;\nand\n\n(b)\nthe provisions of this Act that prohibit disclosure of\ninformation; and\n\n(c)\nthe provisions of the Telecommunications Act 1997 that\nprohibit the disclosure of information.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-167-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-167"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-167-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission to exempt certain acts from provisions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Designated international agreement between Australia and foreign countries.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Exemption granted for acts in compliance with foreign country orders or requests."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-168",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "168 Incoming orders and requests—exemptions from various",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-168"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021.pdf, p.218",
      "values:originalText": "prohibitions\n\nIf:\n\n(a) there is a designated international agreement between\nAustralia and one or more foreign countries; and\n\n(b) the agreement deals with (among other things):\n\n(i) the issue of orders (however described); or\n\n(ii) the making of requests (however described);\n\nby a competent authority (however described) of such a\nforeign country;\nthen:\n\n(c) subsections 7(1) and 108(1) do not apply to or in relation to:\n\n(i) an act or thing done in compliance with such an order or\nrequest; or\n\n(ii) the issue of such an order or the making of such a\nrequest; and\n\n(d) subsections 63(1) and 133(1) do not apply to or in relation to:\n\n(i) an act or thing done in compliance with such an order or\nrequest; or\n\n(ii) information obtained in accordance with such an order\nor request; and\n\n(e) sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act\n1997 do not apply to or in relation to:\n\n(i) an act or thing done in compliance with such an order or\nrequest; or\n\n(ii) information obtained in accordance with such an order\nor request.\nNote 1:\nIn a prosecution for an offence against subsection 7(1) or 108(1), a\ndefendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nparagraph (c): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\nNote 2:\nIn a prosecution for an offence against subsection 63(1) or 133(1), a\ndefendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nparagraph (d): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\nNote 3:\nIn a prosecution for an offence against section 276, 277 or 278 of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997, a defendant bears an evidential burden\nin relation to the matter in paragraph (e): see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021",
      "skos:definition": "prohibitions\n\nIf:\n\n(a) there is a designated international agreement between\nAustralia and one or more foreign countries; and\n\n(b) the agreement deals with (among other things):\n\n(i) the issue of orders (however described); or\n\n(ii) the making of requests (however described);\n\nby a competent authority (however described) of such a\nforeign country;\nthen:\n\n(c) subsections 7(1) and 108(1) do not apply to or in relation to:\n\n(i) an act or thing done in compliance with such an order or\nrequest; or\n\n(ii) the issue of such an order or the making of such a\nrequest; and\n\n(d) subsections 63(1) and 133(1) do not apply to or in relation to:\n\n(i) an act or thing done in compliance with such an order or\nrequest; or\n\n(ii) information obtained in accordance with such an order\nor request; and\n\n(e) sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act\n1997 do not apply to or in relation to:\n\n(i) an act or thing done in compliance with such an order or\nrequest; or\n\n(ii) information obtained in accordance with such an order\nor request.\nNote 1:\nIn a prosecution for an offence against subsection 7(1) or 108(1), a\ndefendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nparagraph (c): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\nNote 2:\nIn a prosecution for an offence against subsection 63(1) or 133(1), a\ndefendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nparagraph (d): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\nNote 3:\nIn a prosecution for an offence against section 276, 277 or 278 of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997, a defendant bears an evidential burden\nin relation to the matter in paragraph (e): see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nGeneral amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 78, 2021\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (International Production\nOrders) Act 2021",
      "cml:asserts": [
