        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-172-ss-5-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021-sch-1-sec-172-ss-5-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ffd172a4aa0b26c7d0d6d2c1f326cda2dcad7869c4cff496e70505ad259e6189",
      "skos:note": "Issuing person must give instrument of cancellation to Australian Designated Authority as soon as practicable after order is cancelled."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-international-production-orders-act-2021#sch-1-sec-172-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "172(5) International production order issued in response to a telephone",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 220,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the international production order is cancelled by the issuing\nperson under subclause (3):\n\n(a) the issuing person must:\n\n(i) give the instrument of cancellation to the Australian\nDesignated Authority; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the order is cancelled;\nand\n\n(b) if the telephone application was made on behalf of a relevant\nagency—the Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(i) inform the chief officer of the relevant agency of the\ncancellation; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of\ncancellation is given to the Australian Designated\nAuthority; and\n\n(c) if the telephone application was made on behalf of the\nOrganisation—the Australian Designated Authority must:\n\n(i) inform the Organisation of the cancellation; and\n\n(ii) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of\ncancellation is given to the Australian Designated\nAuthority.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
